    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d914">

                <pb facs="0833" n="717" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg717"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/2754.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American
                    Ambassador</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-02-07T13:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 7, 1912—1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>It is possible that in case of a sudden emergency the patrol along the border may
                    be strengthened; the Army has been notified to be prepared for border patrol
                    duty. But these are only precautionary steps, and the President’s attitude is
                    identical with his attitude as expressed in his message to Congress last
                    year.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
